04:47:33 said  I've rebuilt the Scale Optimizer so it works like the original. I worked from your signed-in portal's own code, because the pop-ups wouldn't open when the recording tool clicked them in your Chrome.
04:47:33 said  - **Recommendations:** clicking a row, or its "Fix once" button, now opens the "Scale Optimizer details" pop-up. It shows the stats, the rule used and the suggested action, each with a button to see more. From there, Fix once asks you to confirm, then shows "Resolved successfully" with Undo and an offer to automate or review similar issues in the same ad group. Ignore also asks first now.
04:47:33 said  - **Manage:** the pencil opens the full "Edit Scale Optimizer" window, the same one "Create new" opens. In it you pick the rule, choose one of 5 card colours, turn ad group signals on or off, switch the optimizer on or off, and see a live card preview. Delete asks "Are you sure?", and Bulk edit can delete, turn off or turn on the selected optimizers.
04:47:33 said  - **History:** you can now restore a bid, unignore a keyword, revert several changes at once and use date presets.
04:47:33 said  I tested each of these in a browser and they ran without errors.
04:47:33 said  **Still different or unknown:**
04:47:33 said  - I couldn't see the original pop-ups, so their exact look is unconfirmed, though their sizes and colours come from the original's style settings.
04:47:33 said  - The "See calculations" text and the tooltip that lists each rule's conditions are my own wording, not the portal's.
04:47:33 said  - The automatic likeness check (68%) compares against the empty debugging page rather than your portal, so it doesn't tell us anything here.
04:47:34 said  If you send screenshots of a Recommendations row's details pop-up and the Edit window from the real portal, I can match them exactly.
